WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.930
CHARLES VEST: OpenCourseWare
is a web-based program

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.520
that will provide free access to
primary materials for virtually

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.627
every course at MIT.

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:12.210
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL:
The founders of OCW

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.470
had a transformative vision 20
years ago of offering access

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.955
to materials from the MIT
classroom openly, freely.

00:00:20.955 --> 00:00:23.580
CURT NEWTON: They can learn from
them straight off the website.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.130
They can download them
and carry them around.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.070
They can remix them with
other kinds of materials,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.660
mash them up in new ways.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.767
They can share them
with their networks.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.100
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL: We're
getting about 22 million visits

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.940
per year.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.400
We have more than 3
million subscribers

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.870
to the OCW YouTube channel.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:44.190
It makes it the biggest .edu
YouTube channel in the world.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.310
CURT NEWTON: It has captured
curious learners of all stripes

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.832
from around the world.

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:50.790
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL: Several
thousand MIT faculty

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:54.033
have shared materials from
more than 2,500 courses.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.950
CURT NEWTON: We're sharing
materials, not just

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.770
from the science, technology,
engineering, and math courses

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.830
and the management courses
that MIT is most famous, for

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.900
but also from the incredible
richness of our humanities

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.150
and social sciences.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.650
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL:
The impact of OCW

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.900
in opening learning for
millions around the world

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.330
is multiplied by the role
of educators elsewhere.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.430
When they take
materials from OCW

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.560
and repurpose them and
use them and make them

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.620
part of their own teaching,
for each one educator that

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.080
does that, there's
dozens or hundreds

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.420
more people for whom the
opportunities to learn

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.448
are opened up.

00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:30.990
CURT NEWTON: It
takes resources to do

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.820
what we do at OpenCourseWare.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.810
It takes a lot of people and
time and energy and money

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.065
to cover the full
curriculum at MIT.

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:41.940
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL: We
are right in the middle

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.630
of building the next-generation
platform for OCW.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.400
We expect to roll it
out within a few months.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.960
It will be mobile-friendly.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.690
It will have much
better search tools.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.820
What we teach it at
MIT changes with time.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.840
How we teach changes with time.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.900
We need a new platform
that will allow

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.490
us to keep the content at
OCW current and vibrant.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.890
CURT NEWTON: Knowledge should
be free, and especially

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.340
knowledge that comes from
leading institutions,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.070
institutions with the most
privilege behind them.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.410
To give that back to
the world has never

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.120
been more important
than it is today.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.990
So many of the challenges
that the world is facing

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.830
require the development, the
application, the testing,

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.610
the refinement of new
forms of knowledge.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.200
KRISHNA RAJAGOPAL:
We firmly believe

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.200
that a world in which the
educational attainment

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.510
of millions of people
has been elevated

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:35.920
will be a better world.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.050
This is making a difference.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.400
[MUSIC PLAYING]

